.env
*.sqlite3
# Timestamped database backups do not match `*.sqlite3`.
*.sqlite3.bak*
*.sqlite3-*

# NOTE: `locale/**/*.mo` is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# Django reads compiled catalogues, not `.po` files, so a checkout without
# the `.mo` renders every page in the source language no matter what the
# language switch says. Committing it is what lets `web/test_i18n.py` assert
# from a clean CI checkout that French really reaches the page. The Render
# build command still runs `compilemessages`, so a `.po` edit can never ship
# alongside a stale binary — the committed `.mo` is a floor, not the
# mechanism.
#
# Regenerate both together:
#   python manage.py makemessages -l fr \
#       --ignore=.venv-linux --ignore=node_modules --ignore=staticfiles
#   python scripts/translate_fr.py locale/fr/LC_MESSAGES/django.po
#   python manage.py compilemessages
#
# There is deliberately no `locale/en`: English is the source language, so
# its msgid *is* the string and a catalogue for it could only say the same
# thing twice.